      {
        "text": "# Pipeline\n\nA **pipeline** is a series of steps that you run in order, where the output from one step becomes the input to the next. \n\nPipelines are often used to process lists of items, like posts, videos, or comments.\n\nFor a video site, you might:\n1. Filter out videos that are too old,\n2. Sort the remaining videos by score,\n3. Map the top 3 videos into cards on the homepage.\n\nTogether, those steps form a pipeline.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/bc8e2ff48b33e6563490536a83a6a1f0-Screenshot 2025-11-21 135710.png",
        "key": "undefined-ea03636a-a1b5-4568-be2b-86c3c6462665",
